Wire the HarmonyOS OHAudio microphone stream into Chromium audio capture.

The implementation is new code under overlay/media/audio/ohos/, so this patch
only adds those files to the existing OHOS source list in media/audio/BUILD.gn.
libohaudio is already linked by chromium-154-harmonyos.patch for audio output.

Generated for Chromium 154.0.8037.51 after chromium-154-harmonyos.patch. Apply
this patch once to a persistent runner whose main adapter patch is already
present:

  git -C /path/to/chromium/src apply /path/to/patches/ohos-audio-input.patch

diff --git a/media/audio/BUILD.gn b/media/audio/BUILD.gn
--- a/media/audio/BUILD.gn
+++ b/media/audio/BUILD.gn
@@ -299,5 +299,7 @@ source_set("audio") {
       "ohos/audio_manager_ohos.cc",
       "ohos/audio_manager_ohos.h",
+      "ohos/ohos_audio_input.cc",
+      "ohos/ohos_audio_input.h",
       "ohos/ohos_audio_output.cc",
       "ohos/ohos_audio_output.h",
     ]
